! SIC PREFIXED TO BD STORES THE COUNTER INTO A PROTECTED WORD -- the
! interruption-table entry "SIC,STIC / BD,SIFAE", taken while a problem
! program runs under its own boundaries.  StretchExecute's Sic arm,
! 2026-11-19.
!
! THE PAGES (Reference Manual 22-6530-2, read in the page images):
!   printed p.31 (PDF 35): "When the interruption system is disabled,
!   address monitoring is ineffective.  In the disabled mode, core
!   storage protection as specified by the address boundary registers
!   in conjunction with the boundary control bit does not take place".
!   printed p.41 (PDF 44): SIC "is executed if and only if the
!   associated branching is successful".
!   printed p.49 (PDF 52): the table entry for a short correction routine
!   is "an unconditional STORE INSTRUCTION COUNTER IF BRANCH DISABLED
!   instruction to the subroutine ... storing the counter in a suitable
!   address".
!   MCP's own table, MCP_Mar63_001-249 printed p.111 ll.2-3 (PDF 118):
!   SIT+21 is SIC,STIC / BD,SIFAE, STIC at 215265 in MCP's area.  A PP
!   runs with boundaries that protect everything outside its limits
!   (CRETBU, printed p.142 ll.41-51, loads them from SLRBU), so every
!   IF trap from a PP stores into a protected word.
!
! THE BUG.  The Sic arm tested the store with protViolates, i.e. against
! the enable state BEFORE the inner BD, and so suppressed the store and
! raised DS.  Found by tests/check_bss_mcp_go.py stage 7 (2026-11-19):
! *MAIN*'s B,$MCP / ,$EOJ trapped IF, STIC kept the previous trap's
! counter (resume load's ,SDRET), DS came on, and MCP's SIFAE analyzed
! the old $RET again.
!
! RECONSTRUCTION (the pages do not say it in one sentence): when the
! inner branch is BD, the SIC store is not monitored -- the system is
! disabled after it.  Otherwise the store is tested as before, against
! the state before the branch.  So SIC with BE/BEW from the disabled state
! still stores unmonitored (no page decides that case; it is unchanged
! from the model before this deck, and case 2 pins it).  It follows the
! reading the model already uses for the branch target itself
! (ifViolatesAfter, the BE/BD/BEW arm), and it is the only one under which
! MCP's printed table works for a PP.
!
! CASES (bit k of RES = the event in case k):
!   0  enabled, SIC,PROTA / BD,TA, PROTA protected:
!      DS stays off (RES.0 = 0), PROTA.0-18 = the counter (CASEA+1.0)
!   1  enabled, SIC,PROTB / B,TB, PROTB protected, stays enabled
!      (CONTROL): DS interrupts (table entry 19 sets RES.1 = 1) and
!      PROTB stays 0.
!   2  DISABLED, SIC,PROTC / BE,TC, PROTC protected (run between 0 and 1):
!      the model's behaviour before this deck, unchanged and pinned -- the
!      store is made (PROTC.0-18 = the counter) and DS stays off.  No page
!      decides it; if DS came on, the BE would take it at once (to DSR).
!
! INJECTIONS (MEASURED 2026-11-19, StretchExecute's Sic arm, the test's
! enable argument; observed):
!   the bug restored (st.irqEnabled(), the pre-BD state): 4 fail -- RES
!     0xc000000000000000 (case 0 raised DS), PROTA 0, CYCLES 299,
!     MEMREADS 25.  PROTB, PROTC and PC pass.
!   the state after the branch alone (enAfter): 3 fail -- PROTC 0 (case
!     2's store suppressed), CYCLES 282, MEMREADS 24.  RES passes: the BE
!     takes the DS at once and DSR's RES.1 is case 1's bit.
!   the store never tested (False): 4 fail -- RES 0 and PROTB
!     0x0213e00000000000 (the control case stored), CYCLES 348, MEMREADS
!     25.  PROTA, PROTC and PC pass.
!   Control: the fixed model, all 7 pass.  CYCLES and MEMREADS are MODEL
!   behaviour, not printed times.
!
        SLC, (8)4100.0
START   BD,  $+.32                   ! run disabled
        LVI, $X13, TBL
        SV,  $X13, $IA               ! interruption address := TBL
        LWF(U), BNDA
        ST(BU), $UB, 64              ! protect PROTA only
        BE,  $+.32                   ! enable
CASEA   SIC, PROTA
        BD,  TA
        NOP
TA      BZB, $DS, TA1
        BB1, RES+.0, $+1.0           ! case 0 raised DS (must not)
TA1     LWF(U), BNDC                 ! (disabled, after BD,TA)
        ST(BU), $UB, 64              ! protect PROTC only
CASEC   SIC, PROTC
        BE,  TC
        NOP
TC      BZB, $DS, TC1
        BB1, RES+.2, $+1.0           ! case 2 raised DS (must not)
TC1     BD,  $+.32                   ! disable again
        LWF(U), BNDB
        ST(BU), $UB, 64              ! protect PROTB only
        BE,  $+.32                   ! enable
CASEB   SIC, PROTB
        B,   TB
TB      NOP
        BD,  $+.32
        B,   PASS
PASS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)6000.0
BNDA    VF,  PROTA+1.0               ! upper (bits 0-17)
        VF,  PROTA                   ! lower (bits 32-49), control bit 0:
                                     !   the area inside is protected
BNDB    VF,  PROTB+1.0
        VF,  PROTB
BNDC    VF,  PROTC+1.0
        VF,  PROTC
        SLC, (8)6100.0
RES     DD, 0
PROTA   DD, 0
PROTB   DD, 0
PROTC   DD, 0
        SLC, (8)6200.0
TBL     DD, 0
        SLC, (8)6223.0
DSRTN   BD,  DSR                     ! entry 19 = DS
        SLC, (8)6300.0
DSR     BB1, RES+.1, $+1.0
        BDSZ, $+.32                  ! DS off
        B,   PASS
        END, START
